== Live coverage ==
COTF is [[Sports broadcasting|broadcast]] on [[YouTube]] and [[Motorsport.tv]] with live footage, [[sports commentator|commentary]], and interviews for all competitive sessions.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.kartcom.com/en/news/2025/01/30/champions-of-the-future-academy-program-2025-a-springboard-to-the-top-of-international-karting/ |title=Champions of the Future Academy Program 2025: A springboard to the top of international karting |date=30 January 2025 |website=Kartcom |access-date=9 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250710003354/https://www.kartcom.com/en/news/2025/01/30/champions-of-the-future-academy-program-2025-a-springboard-to-the-top-of-international-karting/ |archive-date=10 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> The final round of the 2025 Shifters at [[Autodromo di Franciacorta|Franciacorta]] had a record viewership of over 19 thousand people,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.youtube.com/@championskarting/streams |title=Champions of the Future {{!}} Live |website=[[YouTube]] |publisher=[[Google]] |access-date=18 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251118050445/https://www.youtube.com/@championskarting/streams |archive-date=18 November 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> with over six thousand watching the opening round of the 2024 Academy Program at [[Cremona Circuit|Cremona]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.youtube.com/@ChampionsKartingAcademy/streams |title=Champions of the Future Academy Program {{!}} Live |website=[[YouTube]] |publisher=[[Google]] |access-date=10 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250710032932/https://www.youtube.com/@ChampionsKartingAcademy/streams |archive-date=10 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Apex Timing provides live timing for each COTF event, including free practice and all competitive sessions, via their website.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://theracebox.com/champions-of-the-future-guide-to-round-1-at-zuera |title=Champions of the Future : Guide to Round 1 at Zuera |last=Alvarez |first=Guillaume |date=16 July 2020 |website=The RaceBox |access-date=7 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240913191230/https://theracebox.com/champions-of-the-future-guide-to-round-1-at-zuera |archive-date=13 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

