== Driver development programme ==
In August 2025, RGMMC—in partnership with its [[sister company]] ''Motorsport Performance Academy''—announced the creation of the '''Champions of the Future Racing Academy''', a year-long [[driver development programme]] led by [[Augusto Farfus]] with extensive [[Formula 4]] testing for drivers in their final season of kart racing.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.kartcom.com/en/news/2025/09/02/champions-of-the-future-launches-groundbreaking-f4-racing-academy |title=Champions of the Future Launches Groundbreaking F4 Racing Academy |date=2 September 2025 |website=Kartcom |access-date=8 September 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250908211916/https://www.kartcom.com/en/news/2025/09/02/champions-of-the-future-launches-groundbreaking-f4-racing-academy |archive-date=8 September 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> The COTFA champions will additionally receive test sessions, with the {{nowrap|[[OK-N]]}} champion receiving an F4 test and the {{nowrap|[[OKN-J]]}} champion a [[legends car]] test.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.kartcom.com/en/news/2025/10/20/champions-of-the-future-academy-program-a-springboard-to-professional-motorsport |title=Champions of the Future Academy Program: a springboard to professional motorsport |date=20 October 2025 |website=Kartcom |access-date=13 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251113141756/https://www.kartcom.com/en/news/2025/10/20/champions-of-the-future-academy-program-a-springboard-to-professional-motorsport |archive-date=13 November 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

